# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
#
# Kernel configuration for Unisoc UMS9620 (T760) devices.
#
# The SoC is not a mainline platform: this tree carries the MU300 project's port
# (patches-6.18/0000-sprd-ums9620-port.patch, the drivers of Unisoc's 5.4 vendor
# kernel moved to the 6.18 API) and the rest of its kernel patches, and the
# values below are that port's tested configuration (mu300-linux
# upstream/mu300-mainline.config for Linux 6.18.60, which is the version this
# tree builds).
#
# It is the *resolved* configuration, not their fragment. mu300-linux merges a
# fragment onto allnoconfig and lets `olddefconfig` fill in the rest; OpenWrt
# writes .config and hands it to kbuild, whose syncconfig then asks for every
# promptable symbol the file does not name - and a build has no terminal, so it
# stops at the first one. Every symbol whose value differs from
# generic/config-6.18 is therefore written out here (kb/make-config.py of that
# session generated it; regenerate the same way when bumping the kernel).
# Toolchain probes (CC_*, GCC_VERSION, *_VERSION, HAVE_*, ARCH_HAS_* ...) are
# left out on purpose: they have to follow the toolchain, not this file.
#
# What must stay, whatever changes:
#  - CONFIG_CMDLINE_FORCE: the bootloader's command line is not read (LK passes
#    nothing usable), and rdinit=/init is what starts the MU300 initramfs.
#  - CONFIG_RANDOMIZE_BASE unset: LK loads the kernel at a fixed address and the
#    wrapped Image (see image/wrap-image.py) branches to a fixed offset.
#  - CONFIG_SERIAL_SPRD + earlycon at 0x20210000: the only console, on ttyS1.
#  - ARCH_SPRD with the UMS9620 clock, pinctrl, PMIC/regulator, sdhci, USB and
#    PCIe drivers built in: the initramfs loads no modules for these.
#  - ARM64_4K_PAGES / ARM64_PA_BITS_48 / CPU_LITTLE_ENDIAN: the generic config
#    leaves the first two unset and sets the last one to n, and a choice without
#    a value is what made syncconfig prompt.
#
# BTF is not in this file: the tested build has CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF (its eBPF
# programs, dae for one, need it) and MODULE_ALLOW_BTF_MISMATCH, and OpenWrt owns
# those symbols through CONFIG_KERNEL_DEBUG_INFO_BTF (which builds host pahole).
